# The backplane computer (hw/design.md), as far as the emulator models it:
# the CPU and north bridge card, 1 MB of RAM on the backplane, and the
# flash. Step 1 of the emulator plan; the cards come later.
#
# The north bridge maps the CPU's 64 KB through four 16 KB windows. At reset
# W0-W2 are RAM blocks 0-2 and W3 is the top 16 KB of ROM A, read-only, so
# the BIOS starts in flash and shadows itself into bank F (hw/design.md,
# "Boot"). Its registers are at $C680. Add `bootsel` to start with W3 on RAM
# block 63 instead, as when the bus spy has loaded RAM. The bridge owns the
# DS3231 real-time clock (ds3231.h), which starts at the host's local time;
# its tick interrupts as module D.
#
# The flash image is the whole 512 KB ROM A (as a programmer would write
# it), with the BIOS in its top 16 KB: block 31, $7C000-$7FFFF. The CPU
# sees $C800-$FFFF of it; $C000-$C7FF is the I/O hole.
#
# ROM B (module 5) is the cartridge, erased flash until something is
# plugged in: `emulator --apple-rom FILE` (the owner's Apple IIe ROM, 16 KB,
# or CD,EF) puts a IIe ROM at its start, for the BIOS's C806R to copy into
# bank E before entering Apple II mode.
#
# The DMA controller (module 8, $C400) takes the bus from the CPU for its
# transfers; CONTROL starts at $70, so software turns it on. No card that
# requests DMA is modelled yet; memory-to-memory copies work.
#
# The Console card (module E, $C700) is the front panel: switches, lights,
# HALT/CONT and a breakpoint on any bus cycle. Without a panel attached (the
# terminal emulator has none) programs can still use its breakpoint and
# HALT, which stop at the debugger.
#
# The video card (module 9, $C480) draws VGA 640x480 (video_card.h). It
# powers up with the display off: software sets the palette, a layer and
# CTRL. `emulator --screen FILE` saves its last frame. Revision 1 (rev=1,
# today's BIOS and OODOS) draws from banks 8-B, which it snoops. Revision 2
# (hw/video-rev2.md, proposed: rev=2, or MachineOptions::video_revision)
# draws from 2 MB of its own memory, reached through the aperture line,
# physical bank 8, which the card then answers over RAM C (banks 9-B stay
# RAM), and through its data port, on DMA channel 1 (drq=1). On revision 1
# the aperture line is inert and the card never asks for DMA.
#
# The USB card (module B, $C580) is the keyboard, mouse and game port
# (usb_card.h). Nothing types on it in the terminal app; the WebUI does.
#
# The sound card (module A, $C500) holds two SIDs and 64 KB for a 6510 of
# its own (sound_card.h): so far its registers, RAM and mailbox. RAMDATA is
# on DMA channel 2.
#
# The mass storage card (module 7, $C380) is an SD card behind an RP2350
# (sd_card.h): sectors through DATA, by CPU or DMA channel 0. `emulator --sd
# FILE` puts a card image in its slot, written through.
#
# The serial card (module 6, $C300): its TL16C552A isn't modelled yet, so
# the terminal is a STAND-IN, a 6551 at $C300-$C303 (mirrored through the
# block, as before: the BIOS and OODOS use $C300-$C303 only). The card's
# W65C22S VIA is real (via6522.h), at $C340-$C34F: the later line answers
# there, over the 6551's mirror. Both pull IRQL bit 6 (module 6). The
# card's INTSTAT ($C322) isn't modelled: $C322 is still the 6551's mirror
# (its command register), so a handler tells the VIA by its IFR. The VIA's
# ports are the two joysticks (joystick_ports.h): joystick 1 on PA0-PA4,
# joystick 2 on PB0-PB4, up/down/left/right/fire, 0 when pressed; the
# rest pulled up, so `LDA $C341` `AND #$1F` reads $1F with nothing pressed.
# The WebUI drives them from gamepads or its keys; the terminal app's
# debugger has `joy`.
#
#   emulator --machine machines/backplane.machine bios.rom

cpu          w65c02s
northbridge  backplane

ram   00000-3FFFF  module=0  name=ram_a     # RAM A-D: 256 KB each, A18-A19
ram   40000-7FFFF  module=1  name=ram_b
ram   80000-BFFFF  module=2  name=ram_c
ram   C0000-FFFFF  module=3  name=ram_d
rom   00000-7FFFF  space=flash  module=4  name=rom_a  bios.rom
rom   80000-FFFFF  space=flash  module=5  name=rom_b  -   # the cartridge: empty unless --apple-rom

# The VIA's line must come after the 6551's: the later mapping answers
# (test_joyports checks it).
acia6551  300-37F  space=io  name=terminal  irq     # stand-in serial card
via6522   340-34F  space=io  name=via  irq          # the serial card's VIA, over the 6551's mirror
joyports  name=joysticks  via=via                    # on PA0-4 and PB0-4
sd        380-3FF  space=io  name=sd  irq  drq=0
dma       400-47F  space=io  name=dma  irq
video     480-4FF  space=io  name=video  irq  drq=1  rev=1
aperture  80000-8FFFF  module=9  name=aperture   # revision 2: bank 8 is the card's
sound     500-57F  space=io  name=sound  irq  drq=2
usb       580-5FF  space=io  name=usb  irq
disk2     600-67F  space=io  name=disk2               # slot 6 in Apple II mode
console   700-77F  space=io  name=console  irq     # the front panel
